sentences.t:
Mándot que vayas con ellas fata dentro en Carrión,
verás las heredades que a mis fijas dadas son;
con aquestas nuevas vernás al Campeador.”

sentences.l:
I-order-you that you-go with them as-far-as inside in Carrión,
you-will-see the estates that to my daughters given are;
with these news you-will-come to-the Campeador.”

Minaya Álbar Fáñez before my Çid himself stopped:
“Let-us-turn-back, Çid, to Valençia the great;
for if to God it-should-please and to-the Father Creator,
go them we-will to-see to lands of Carrión.”

sentences.t:
Piénssanse de ir ifantes de Carrión;
por Santa María d’ Alvarrazín la posada [fecho fo],
aguijan quanto pueden ifantes de Carrión;
félos en Molina con el moro Avengalvón.

sentences.l:
Set-themselves to go Infantes of Carrión;
by Santa María of Alvarrazín the lodging [made was],
they-spur as-much-as they-can Infantes of Carrión;
behold-them in Molina with the Moor Avengalvón.

sentences.t:
El moro quando lo sopo, plógol de coraçón;
saliólos recebir con grandes avorozes;
Dios, que bien los sirvió a todo so sabor!

sentences.l:
The Moor when it he-learned, it-pleased-him from heart;
went-out-them to-receive with great rejoicings;
God, how well them he-served to all their pleasure!

sentences.t:
A las fijas del Çid el moro sus donas dió,
buenos seños cavallos a ifantes de Carrión;
tod esto les fizo el moro por el amor del Çid Campead[or].

sentences.l:
To the daughters of-the Çid the Moor his gifts gave,
good one-each horses to Infantes of Carrión;
all this to-them did the Moor for the love of-the Çid Campead[or].

“Now since that to abandon we-have daughters of-the Campeador,
if we-could kill the Moor Avengalvón,
as-much wealth as he-has have it we-would we.

sentences.t:
Quando esta falssedad dizien los de Carrión,
un moro latinado bien gelo entendió;
non tiene poridad, díxolo Avengalvón:

sentences.l:
When this falsehood were-saying those of Carrión,
a Moor latin-speaking well it-to-him understood;
not he-keeps secret, said-it Avengalvón:
